unit JoinGuard;

{
  JoinGuard - catches (and repairs) the host crash when a player joins a
              battle room that already has 10+ players.

  Network_Add_Player_Remote (0x450A10) runs on the host when a player joins.
  With 10+ players in the room the game ends up executing at a bad address a
  few bytes after one of this function's calls (0x450D0C / 0x450D15 / 0x450D20
  / 0x000E0D0B), with EBX/EBP still holding this function's early values -
  i.e. one of its calls returns somewhere it should not, with a broken stack.

  Every call this function makes on the way is redirected to a stub that
  keeps the real return address and the caller's EBX/EBP/ESI/EDI in its own
  storage (so the callee cannot damage them), calls the real function, and
  then checks ESP and those registers. If anything is off it logs which call
  did it to tplayx_joinguard.log, puts everything back and returns to the
  right place.

  Generated by C:\tpLAYX1\tools\gen_joinguard.py - edit that, not this.
  Off switch without rebuilding: empty file  joinguard.off  in the game folder.
}

